{"title":"2023 OIM Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/2517f5ec989d271e331cabd8205141900323fbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, \\cdots , P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> of points in the plane (not necessarily distinct) is \"<i>carioca</i>\" if there exists a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/b/c7b6ccb7f7b30fbca66a9159e022a13677d4f0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\cdots , a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5ef3fd61ef0547d6307e6ae6a97f9a9517510f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, \\cdots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> such that all the segments\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fcab7ede7696e046a0761cb3e6c847a56e518dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_{a1}P_{a2},P_{a2}P_{a3},\\cdots,P_{an}P_{a1}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>have the same length. Find the largest number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that for any sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> points in the plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eee3e7c78ee8dbc3060ce971b24f237d2c841b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> points can be added so that the sequence of 2023 points is <i>carioca</i>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c237ad93345fe64723c92fdcd8c06703988f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>In general, if the problem statement is \"find the largest number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that for any sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> points in the plane, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712b864e0677c83ccc58a518749adf654ae921d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N-1-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> points can be added so that the sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef697bdf674123e9ee81feb014414987b072a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> points is carioca,\" the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27fa8a149d9c488724150c97368728c88d41155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le N.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For a counterexample with higher <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038008fb83bbb21fdb2aa33a19e967f9c18543c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, consider a sequence of points in a straight line such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/73365bc82325400b5a485708f41266f7f0dc3c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1P_2 = 1, ... , P_nP_{n+1} = 2^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a794b521417af3632f9ed3dac2fc363e3e90431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le n &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. Notice that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7bb045e911c5cdef7504f7ed7b2912b1f30ab70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_aP_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> are distinct for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />. In the sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f1322bda9c5264eba11202a86c6af25dc539a010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{a_1}, \\dots P_{a_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" />, we are not able to place enough points (we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> spaces to fill after we chose a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7bb045e911c5cdef7504f7ed7b2912b1f30ab70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_aP_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> common point distance for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712b864e0677c83ccc58a518749adf654ae921d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N-1-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> points, not enough since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038008fb83bbb21fdb2aa33a19e967f9c18543c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />). Contradiction, since all points must have the same distance.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11afb49a798b4d55aec61ed0d04445d39763d9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\le N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec341f78804b81f7a1c4152e2cf9c6a9761d3aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, \\dots, P_N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> be our points (if we have fewer, place the remaining ones at random). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d874e17c7ea25b97dc858c88374b891b2a6f6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/15245bc6e388de68e6fa07b00f49b5386c770d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be points such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72eee661de75948b7bfaf819178a71ba115af31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_aP_b=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" /> is maximal. Choose a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c93898b56e82ef5ac03026823a6ecff6ccc3b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_a, \\dots, P_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. Between each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1c502923b9bf61c1bc239667bd5aca980f4b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de06b166301e15e67e0e984266544ed6302e241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i &lt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" />, place a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fb3046ae7fe9fa4cab4dd81d20b8922e1bae74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_iQ = QP_{i+1} = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />. This triangle is a valid isosceles triangle since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is maximal. Since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> holes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/712b864e0677c83ccc58a518749adf654ae921d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2N-1-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> points, we have enough as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04538d729cbeeee061f2de4af177d714e2897b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://sites.google.com/associacaodaobm.org/oim-brasil-2023/pruebas\">https://sites.google.com/associacaodaobm.org/oim-brasil-2023/pruebas</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6790/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26144:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018023728 and revision id 282597. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}